From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 08:59:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ARMJIT_A64: LOOPREGS: an ARM9 loop's RegionCodeCycles stored once at its entry

An ARM9 LoopMode block stores RegionCodeCycles for its own page once at its
entry, and the body starts with it known (KnownCode, 0007's CODESTORES): the
taken branches to the same page (the loop's way back, a followed branch inside
it) skip their mov+str every way round (HeartGold's 021f9292T: two a way
round). Each way round still ends with that value in memory (a branch to
another page clears the knowledge, so the branch back stores it again). Only
the interpreter's CodeRead32 reads RegionCodeCycles, after a JumpTo that sets
it. MELONDS_JIT_NOLOOPCODE=1: off.
---
--- a/src/ARMJIT_A64/ARMJIT_Compiler.cpp
+++ b/src/ARMJIT_A64/ARMJIT_Compiler.cpp
@@ -368,6 +368,8 @@ Compiler::Compiler(melonDS::NDS& nds) : Arm64Gen::ARM64XEmitter(), NDS(nds)
         LoopNoFollow = getenv("MELONDS_JIT_NOLOOPFOLLOW") && atoi(getenv("MELONDS_JIT_NOLOOPFOLLOW"));
         // (patch 0384: LoopMode with block transfers of several registers; MELONDS_JIT_NOLOOPMULTI=1 off)
         LoopNoMulti = getenv("MELONDS_JIT_NOLOOPMULTI") && atoi(getenv("MELONDS_JIT_NOLOOPMULTI"));
+        // (patch 0385: an ARM9 loop's RegionCodeCycles stored once at its entry; MELONDS_JIT_NOLOOPCODE=1 off)
+        LoopNoCode = getenv("MELONDS_JIT_NOLOOPCODE") && atoi(getenv("MELONDS_JIT_NOLOOPCODE"));
         // (patch 0381's fix off, to show the hang: MELONDS_JIT_LOOPRELINKOLD=1)
         LoopRelinkOld = getenv("MELONDS_JIT_LOOPRELINKOLD") && atoi(getenv("MELONDS_JIT_LOOPRELINKOLD"));
         OptLazyFlags = OptKeepFlags && !getenv("MELONDS_JIT_NOLAZYFLAGS");
@@ -1652,6 +1654,18 @@ JitBlockEntry Compiler::CompileBlock(ARM* cpu, bool thumb, FetchedInstr instrs[]
                 MOVP2R(LoopTsReg, Num ? &NDS.ARM7Timestamp : &NDS.ARM9Timestamp);
                 break;
             }
+        if (Num == 0 && OptCodeStores && !LoopNoCode)
+        {
+            // (patch 0385) RegionCodeCycles for the loop's own page stored once here, known from the body's start:
+            // its branches back (and any to the same page) skip their store every way round. Every way round ends
+            // with it in memory (a branch to another page clears the knowledge, so the branch back stores it
+            // again). Only the interpreter's CodeRead32 reads it, after a JumpTo that sets it first.
+            const u32 v = ((ARMv5*)cpu)->MemTimings[instrs[0].Addr >> 12][0];
+            MOVI2R(W0, v);
+            STR(INDEX_UNSIGNED, W0, RCPU, offsetof(ARMv5, RegionCodeCycles));
+            KnownCodeValid = true;
+            KnownCodeValue = v;
+        }
         LoopBodyRX = (u8*)GetRXPtr();
         if (OptLazyFlags)
             CPSRDirty = true;   // (the way round may leave RCPSR out of memory: every exit stores it)
--- a/src/ARMJIT_A64/ARMJIT_Compiler.h
+++ b/src/ARMJIT_A64/ARMJIT_Compiler.h
@@ -310,6 +310,7 @@ public:
                                   // it uses in host registers round the loop (LoopMode)
     bool LoopNoTs = false, LoopNoSigned = false, LoopNoLazy = false, LoopNoXfer = false;   // (LOOPREGS's parts)
     bool LoopNoFollow = false;    // MELONDS_JIT_NOLOOPFOLLOW=1: patch 0382 off (no LoopMode with a branch followed when taken)
+    bool LoopNoCode = false;      // MELONDS_JIT_NOLOOPCODE=1: patch 0385 off
     bool LoopNoMulti = false;     // MELONDS_JIT_NOLOOPMULTI=1: patch 0384 off
     bool LoopR15Back = false;     // (0382: the LoopMode block being compiled stores R15 on its way round)
     bool LoopRelinkOld = false;   // MELONDS_JIT_LOOPRELINKOLD=1: patch 0381 off (a restored LoopMode block relinks to its entry)
